Z||000005||prtzlboy||10-12-2001||07:58 PM||||oh geez no!  Wax that baby all you want.  I wish more people would wax their cars, it adds YEARS to the life of their paint.  Also, I've heard so many people tell me that their dealer told them NOT to wax their car because of the "special clearcoat".  BULLS**T.  Wax it, wax it again, then wax it one more time just for kicks.||||reg||14
Z||000006||rogergarrison||10-13-2001||02:48 PM||||I never wax my car at all. just spray on clear water and towell it off. once in a while i use a little polish or glaze, not wax. And my car always looks fine. To much wax will build up and dull the paint. Dont believe anything about a good wax job really beads the water. A brand new paint job only hours old beads the same way. By not waxing, i can always touch up without it coming back off or fisheyeing and the water runs off instead of leaving all those little circles on it. BTW, I own my own paint&body shop for years in case you dont know.<P>But to each their own. only thing is dont wax if its cold out, or in direct sunlite. Nite is Ok, but awful hard to see what your doing.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=11878523&p=52990885"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||85ZainoGT||10-13-2001||07:01 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>I never wax my car at all. just spray on clear water and towell it off. once in a while i use a little polish or glaze, not wax. And my car always looks fine. To much wax will build up and dull the paint. Dont believe anything about a good wax job really beads the water. A brand new paint job only hours old beads the same way. By not waxing, i can always touch up without it coming back off or fisheyeing and the water runs off instead of leaving all those little circles on it. BTW, I own my own paint&body shop for years in case you dont know.<P>But to each their own. only thing is dont wax if its cold out, or in direct sunlite. Nite is Ok, but awful hard to see what your doing.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>  You own your own body/paint shop?  How bout helping a fellow fiero owner out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I got a few places that needs some fixin up and nice new paint job  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1985 White/Silver GT <BR>2.8L 4 Speed LOADED  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sigpic2529_1.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by 85ZainoGT (edited 10-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||10-13-2001||09:52 PM||||I already have a restoration project im on for quite a while plus my reg dealers. If you want orig color in basecoat/clearcoat urathane, you do all the sanding and trim removing that you want. Then bring it and leave it for about 1 week. Ill do the masking and primer and buy paint for around $600. You finish wet sand and buff. I only do them assembled, so just take off wing, trim, lites etc.I Dont do any disassembled cars for that kind of money. If you do all the same work yourself, Maacos do a pretty fair job for $300 or so and you could get it done there. You can go to their lots and check some of theirs out to pick which one.||||reg||1
